                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "\ud83d\udea8I continue to closely monitor reports of harassment and intimidation against brave Cuban students by university authorities, members of the Communist Party, and the so-called student federation (FEU) at institutions like ISA, FAMCA, ISDI, and Medical Sciences in Santiago, among others.\n\nThese young men and women have shown tremendous courage by speaking out against tyranny. I applaud their bravery and moral clarity in standing up to a brutal regime that has silenced generations before them.\n\nLet me be clear: the world is watching. I strongly urge the Cuban regime\u2014and all those complicit\u2014to stop the intimidation, listen to the students, and respect their call for freedom, dignity, and democracy.\n\nThe courage of these students is not just admirable\u2014it\u2019s historic. And they will not be alone.",
